Description: Fix 450.soplex build failure with GCC >= 11 (C++11+)
 std::istream::getline() returns std::istream&, not void*.
 In C++11 the implicit void* conversion was removed, so == 0 fails.
 Use operator! instead, which works across all C++ standards.
Origin: manual, based on SPEC CPU2006 v1.2 450.soplex
Bug: https://www.spec.org/cpu2006/Docs/faq.html#Build

--- a/benchspec/CPU2006/450.soplex/src/mpsinput.cc
+++ b/benchspec/CPU2006/450.soplex/src/mpsinput.cc
@@ -72,7 +72,7 @@
       // Read until we have a not comment line.
       do
       {
-         if (m_input.getline(m_buf, sizeof(m_buf)) == 0)
+         if (!m_input.getline(m_buf, sizeof(m_buf)))
             return false;
         m_lineno++;
